## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a practical, testable fair-use layer for a multi-tenant LLM gateway with billing considerations.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant quotas and burst handling using a token bucket
- Isolation of prompts and responses per tenant
- Simple REST API for quota status and consumption
- Observability and a minimal test plan for bucket behavior

## Code Example
```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, refillPerMs) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.refillPerMs = refillPerMs;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }
  tick() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = now - this.lastRefill;
    const refill = Math.floor(elapsed * this.refillPerMs);
    if (refill > 0) {
      this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + refill);
      this.lastRefill = now;
    }
  }
  tryConsume(n = 1) {
    this.tick();
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Threats include prompt tampering and replay, which undermine model safety and tenant isolation. A signed prompt ensures integrity and provenance.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant HMAC keys in a KMS
- Nonce/sequence replay protection
- Key rotation and revocation workflow
- Audit logging and tamper-detection tests
- Latency budget impact and mitigation

## Code Example
```javascript
function signPrompt(tenantId, payload, key) {
  const nonce = crypto.randomBytes(12).toString('hex');
  const mac = crypto.createHmac('sha256', key).update(tenantId + '|' + nonce + '|' + payload).digest('hex');
  return { tenantId, nonce, payload, mac };
}

function verifyPrompt(signed, key) {
  const { tenantId, nonce, payload, mac } = signed;
  // fetch current key for tenantId from KMS in real implementation
  const expectedMac = crypto.createHmac('sha256', key).update(tenantId + '|' + nonce + '|' + payload).digest('hex');
  return mac === expectedMac;
}
```

